# Sprint 40 audit: EnvironmentPostProcessor implementations are discovered via the classic
# META-INF/spring.factories mechanism (SpringFactoriesLoader), not via
# META-INF/spring/<FQN>.imports — that newer mechanism is specific to @AutoConfiguration classes.
# The prior registration file (META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor,
# missing the .imports suffix, and later renamed to add it) was never actually read by Spring Boot
# under either name: ProdEnvironmentValidator has never been wired into any real Spring context
# since it was introduced in Sprint 24 — only its unit tests (which construct it directly,
# bypassing Spring's discovery entirely) ever exercised it. Verified empirically: a real
# `-Dspring.profiles.active=prod` boot with no secrets configured booted successfully (and logged
# the ephemeral-key warnings) both before this fix and with the .imports file alone; only this
# spring.factories registration makes the real boot abort as documented.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.brika.platform.config.ProdEnvironmentValidator
